    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a mix of frustration and curiosity for me—something I had to struggle through years ago but still find strangely intuitive now. My father worked in construction, so numbers were practical but rarely theoretical. I enjoy its structure and problem-solving aspects, which align with my conscientiousness score (high). Still, the abstract nature sometimes leaves gaps where biology or philosophy feel more personal.",
